<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.13.3: Matching Tables, Equations, and Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00289</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.13.3: Matching Tables, Equations, and Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b7d5c22b-532c-44f7-a689-b1aaedbb1b2e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Take turns with your partner to match a graph with each set of <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/699661913d8187811b1278b918742716ff9c136e">matching cards</link>. Eventually all the cards will be sorted into groups of four cards (an equation, situation, table, and graph).</para>
<para>For each match that you find, explain to your partner how you know it’s a match. Ask your partner if they agree with your thinking.</para>
<para>For each match that your partner finds, listen carefully to their explanation. If you disagree, discuss your thinking and work to reach an agreement.</para>

<!--Q#1-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What did you and your partner agree are the cards that match the equation on card 1? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Cards 1, 11, 20, 32</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


